Alembic migrations for entity-flow.

The database URL comes from POSTGRES_URL (environment, or .env at the repo
root) via env.py -- alembic.ini holds no credentials.

    alembic upgrade head                       apply everything
    alembic current                            what this database is at
    alembic check                              fail if models have drifted
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."   draft the next revision
    alembic downgrade -1                       step back one

Autogenerate compares tables, columns, indexes and constraints. It is blind to
functions and triggers, so the entity status-validation trigger is written by
hand -- see 0a9fc379d832_initial_schema.py. Any revision that changes that
trigger must say so explicitly; nothing will catch it for you.

Adopting an existing database that already matches the current models:

    alembic stamp head

That records the revision without running it. Only do this when the schema
really does match; `alembic check` will tell you.
